<article class="env-lemma" id="0H8X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H8X">Lemma <span data-tag="0H8X">10.122.4</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a finite type ring map and $\mathfrak p$ be a prime ideal of $R$. Then the following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R \to S$ is quasi-finite at all primes of $S$ lying over $\mathfrak p$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ is a finite $\kappa (\mathfrak p)$-algebra, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p))$ is a finite set. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Condition (1) says the topology on $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p))$ is discrete (as every point is open). Hence the equivalence of (1), (2), (3) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0ALW" data-tag="0ALW">10.61.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>